        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "description": "End of data pipeline",
            "name": "End"
          },
          "outcomes": {},
          "code": "END",
          "id": "end",
          "inputs": [],
          "type": "END"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {
                "k": 0,
                "max_completion_tokens": 32000,
                "reasoning_effort": "medium"
              },
              "code": "ORA_MODEL_CONFIG_PREMIUM_OPEN_AI_GPT_4_1_MINI",
              "model": "OCI_GPT_5_MINI",
              "modelName": "GPT-5 mini",
              "provider": "CERT_PREMIUM"
            },
            "name": "Summariser"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "SUMMARISER",
          "id": "1764082568988",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1764082568991_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "# Input Data\n\nWhen the {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.isProxyUser}} flag is set to true, input should be taken from:\n\n{{$context.$nodes.GET_PUDS_PERSONAL_SRS.$output}} which defines Service Requests, {{$context.$nodes.GET_PUDS_PERSONAL_ASSETS.$output}} which defines Assets, {{$context.$nodes.GET_PUDS_PERSONAL_WORK_ORDERS.$output}} which defines Work Orders, {{$context.$nodes.GET_PUDS_PERSONAL_CHATS.$output}} which defines Chats and {{$context.$nodes.GET_PUDS_SELF_REGISTRATIONS.$output}} which defines Self Registrations.\n\notherwise, it comes from:\n\n{{$context.$nodes.GET_SRS.$output}} which defines Service Requests, {{$context.$nodes.GET_ASSETS.$output}} which defines Assets, {{$context.$nodes.GET_WORK_ORDERS.$output}} which defines Work Orders, {{$context.$nodes.GET_CHAT_INTERACTIONS.$output}} which defines Chats and  {{$context.$nodes.GET_PERSONAL_SELF_REGISTRATIONS.$output}} which defines Self Registrations.\n\nIgnore objects that are not defined or are in error status.\n\n# Instructions\n\nProvide a summary of the Input Data. Return the data as an array of JSON objects as per the output specification. DO NOT add extra properties to the output data objects. DO NOT invent items to include in the output; everything must be based on the Input Data.\n\nThe number of items to include in the summary is defined by {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.maxItems}}. If this is undefined, 6 items should be returned. A mixture of different types should be included, including all types that are available in the Input Data.\n\n## Building JSON Response Data\n\nUse the data in {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.requestItems}} (the Request Items) to define which objects from the Input Data to include in the summary:\n  * An item of type 'asset-purchased' should result in Assets being included in the summary\n  * An item of type 'service-request-waiting' should result in Service Requests that are WAITING for a response (StatusTypeCd = 'ORA_SVC_WAITING') being included in the summary\n  * An item of type 'service-request-updated' should result in Service Requests with a LastUpdateDate within the past month being included in the summary\n  * An item of type 'work-order-scheduled' should result in Work Orders that have a WoStatusCdMeaning of 'Scheduled' being included in the summary\n  * An item of type 'chat-recent' should result in Chats that have a recent StartTime (within the past month) being included in the summary\n  * An item of type 'self-registration-pending' should result in Self Registrations that have a StatusCd value of ORA_CSS_PENDING being included in the summary. Self Registrations with statuses other than ORA_CSS_PENDING MUST BE IGNORED.\n\nThe roles, disabled and icon fields must be copied exactly from the Request Item which caused the object to be included in the summary.\nThe max field from the Request Item must be used to limit number of each type of object in the response.\nThe type field of the output objects must be set to the Request Item type with the final -<operation> omitted. So types must be in lowercase and singular.\nThe tooltip field in the output objects must be of the form: <object type> - <object ID> - <info> where the object type has all words capitalised and any - (dashes) omitted.\nThe operation field of output objects must always be set to 'detail'.\nThe status field of output objects must show the status of the item and a relative time period, e.g. 'Created 1 week ago', 'Resolved 3 days ago', 'Scheduled in 4 days'\nimageUrl, url and detailsId should be omitted from the output objects.\nDon't include ORA_ lookup codes or links in response data.\n\n### Service Requests\n\nWhen creating output with a type of 'service-request':\n  * The id field of the output must be set to the SrNumber from the Input Data.\n  * The title field of the output must be set to the SrNumber from the Input Data.\n  * The description field of the output must be set to the Title from the Input Data.\n\n### Assets\n\nWhen creating output with a type of 'asset':\n  * The id field of the output must be set to the AssetId from the Input Data.\n  * The title field of the output must be set to the ItemDescription from the Input Data.\n  * The status field should indicate when the Asset was purchased, e.g. 'Purchased 2 weeks ago'\n  * The description field of the output must be set to the Title from the Input Data.\n\n### Work Orders\n\nWhen creating output with a type of 'work-order':\n  * The id field of the output must be set to the WoNumber from the Input Data.\n  * The title field of the output must be set to the WoNumber from the Input Data.\n  * The status field should indicate when the Work Order is scheduled, e.g. 'Scheduled in 3 days'\n  * The description field of the output must be set to the Description from the Input Data.\n\n### Chats\n\nIgnore chats that do not have a Description in the Input Data.\nWhen creating output with a type of 'chat':\n  * The id field of the output must be set to the InteractionId from the Input Data.\n  * The title field of the output must be set to the Description from the Input Data.\n\n### Self Registrations\n\nWhen creating output with a type of 'self-registration-pending':\n  * The id field of the output must be set to the RegistrationId from the Input Data.\n  * The title field of the output must be set to the Name from the Input Data.\n  * The description field of the output must be set to the EmailAddress from the Input Data.\n\n## Sorting Results\n\nOrder the output items according to how important they are:\n  * Items that were updated longer ago are more important than those that were updated recently, but only up until one month ago - items older than that are less important.\n  * Chat Interactions are the most important.\n  * Work Orders are more important than Service Requests and Assets.\n  * Service Requests that are waiting for an update should always be displayed before those with other statuses.\n"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"type\": \"array\",\n  \"items\": {\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n      \"ariaLabel\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n      \"roles\": {\n        \"type\": \"array\",\n        \"items\": { \"type\": \"string\" }\n      },\n      \"tooltip\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n      \"type\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"pattern\": \"^[a-z-]+$\" },\n      \"operation\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n      \"id\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n      \"index\": { \"type\": \"number\" },\n      \"title\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n      \"description\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n      \"status\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n      \"displayId\": { \"type\": \"boolean\" },\n      \"icon\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n      \"imageUrl\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n      \"url\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n      \"params\": { \"type\": \"object\" },\n      \"detailsId\": { \"type\": \"string\" }\n    },\n    \"required\": [\n\"id\",\n      \"index\", \"title\", \"description\", \"status\" \n    ],\n    \"additionalProperties\": false\n  }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
